course: dictionary
lesson: 15670
title: Words that beat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can describe a pain, a sound or a movement. Throbbing describes something that beats again and again, like your heart pumping blood. «My thumb is throbbing after I hit it with a hammer.» The thumb is not dancing or shaking; it is beating with pain, over and over. Read the words around throbbing to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Throbbing can also describe a sound. «The music was throbbing through the walls of the hall.» Music that throbs has a strong, steady beat that you can feel. Try the swap check: if «loud, steady beat» fits in place of throbbing and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Throbbing is also a verb. It is the -ing form of throb, which means to beat strongly. «Her heart was throbbing with excitement as the door opened.» Here throbbing shows what her heart was doing. The word was tells you the action was happening at that moment.
fact: Throbbing means beating again and again, like a pulse.
fact: «A throbbing headache» is a headache that pulses with pain.
fact: Throbbing can describe a strong, steady beating sound, like «throbbing engines».
fact: Throb is the verb; throbbing is its -ing form, as in «My head is throbbing».
fact: A nurse or doctor may ask if your pain is throbbing, because that tells them what kind of pain you have.
exercise: «My thumb is throbbing after I hit it with a hammer.» What does throbbing tell us? | The thumb is very cold | The hammer is heavy and still | A quiet, smooth feeling | *A pain that beats again and again
exercise: «The music was throbbing through the walls of the hall.» What does throbbing mean here? | Silent and still | *Beating with a strong, steady sound | Dripping with water | Whispering very softly
exercise: «Her heart was throbbing with excitement.» Find the word that shows the verb throb in its -ing form. | heart | excitement | was | *throbbing
test: «A throbbing headache kept Sam awake.» What does throbbing mean here? | A headache that has gone away | *A headache that pulses with pain | A headache that is very quiet | A headache that makes you laugh
test: «The drums were throbbing across the field.» Is throbbing a verb here? | Yes, because it is a name for the drums | *Yes, it is the -ing form of throb, showing an action | No, it is a place where people meet | No, it is a colour
exam: «After the fall, Max's knee was throbbing, so the nurse put ice on it.» What does throbbing tell the nurse? | Max is happy about his fall | The ice is throbbing and moving | The nurse is tired and needs a rest | *Max's knee has a pain that beats again and again
